\# PART E — CINEMATIC FLOWER ASSEMBLY ENTRANCE\
\
\## 10. MAIN ENTRANCE ANIMATION CONCEPT\
\
When a visitor first opens the website, the bouquet must look as though it is being freshly arranged by an invisible florist.\
\
Do not display a fully assembled bouquet immediately.\
\
Do not use a simple fade-in or scale-up animation.\
\
Create an actual staged bouquet assembly using the individual 3D flowers, stems, wrapping, and ribbon.\
\
\### Stage 1 — Romantic Night Sky (0–1 seconds)\
\
\- Begin with a black background.\
\- Display the moon.\
\- Display all existing and additional stars.\
\- Stars gently twinkle.\
\- Small pink particles float in the scene.\
\- The bouquet is not yet assembled.\
\
\### Stage 2 — Stems Appear (1–2.5 seconds)\
\
\- Green stems move into the scene individually.\
\- Each stem enters from a different direction.\
\- Stems gradually move toward their final positions.\
\- Use smooth organic motion.\
\- Leaves slowly unfold.\
\- Avoid abrupt transitions.\
\
\### Stage 3 — Flowers Are Arranged (2.5–5 seconds)\
\
\- Pink lilies enter one at a time.\
\- Each flower moves toward its designated position.\
\- Center flowers arrive first.\
\- Surrounding flowers follow.\
\- Flowers rotate naturally while moving.\
\- Petals begin blooming as flowers reach their positions.\
\- Use staggered timing.\
\- Add subtle swaying and secondary motion.\
\
The animation must feel like real flowers being carefully arranged.\
\
\### Stage 4 — Wrapping Paper Forms (5–6.5 seconds)\
\
\- Pink wrapping paper begins appearing around the stems.\
\- Individual paper sections fold into position.\
\- The paper gradually encloses the lower bouquet.\
\- Use realistic folding movement.\
\- Avoid intersecting the flowers.\
\
\### Stage 5 — Ribbon Is Tied (6.5–7.5 seconds)\
\
\- The ribbon wraps around the bouquet.\
\- Bow loops form naturally.\
\- The bow extends prominently outward.\
\- Ribbon tails gently fall into place.\
\- The thicker muted-color gift tag settles into position.\
\- Add subtle secondary motion.\
\
Ensure the ribbon does not disappear inside the wrapping.\
\
\### Stage 6 — Final Reveal (7.5–9 seconds)\
\
\- Pixel particles gather around the bouquet.\
\- Flower petals begin falling.\
\- Stars continue twinkling.\
\- The moon softly glows.\
\- The camera gently settles toward the completed bouquet.\
\- The bouquet begins floating.\
\- Subtle lighting highlights the flowers.\
\- The scene transitions into idle animation.\
\
The default duration is approximately nine seconds.\
\
Administrators must be able to customize the total duration.\
